WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.790
He says he's support and he'll upgrade my wallet.

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:13.026
For a standard recovery-phrase wallet, the phrase is the control key,

00:00:13.026 --> 00:00:17.020
not a support code. Same for your private key. Never send them to anyone.

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:19.920
Even our academy assistant should never ask for them.

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:35.733
Two more danger signs: guaranteed returns, and pressure to pay.

00:00:35.733 --> 00:00:40.211
A screenshot of big profits proves nothing, and doesn't mean you could repeat it.

00:00:40.211 --> 00:00:43.030
If someone rushes you past the normal checks, stop.

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:01.367
Connecting a wallet,

00:01:01.367 --> 00:01:05.558
signing a message and approving access to your assets are different things.

00:01:05.558 --> 00:01:09.245
If you don't understand a signature or approval, don't confirm it.

00:01:09.245 --> 00:01:11.480
No password prompt doesn't mean no risk.

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:28.355
If you think something leaked, stop and use the official security channel.

00:01:28.355 --> 00:01:29.908
Act on what actually leaked.

00:01:29.908 --> 00:01:33.680
Never install remote-control software because a scammer told you to.

00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:46.420
Sharing info to receive money isn't the same as handing over the keys.

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:51.610
Share no secrets. Approve nothing you don't understand. Don't be rushed into paying.

00:01:56.250 --> 00:01:59.767
Eleven episodes done. Is it time to deposit real money?

00:01:59.767 --> 00:02:02.580
The Season 1 finale has a surprising answer.

00:02:03.150 --> 00:02:05.220
Understand first, then act.
